pkg:Evidence_v1_53_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.53.0 (real gap corrected: on-the-fly code generation honestly tracked, mission no longer falsely eligible)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: owner directly challenged the prior turn's 'eligible for closure' finding, correctly identifying that on-the-fly code generation reliability was never measured by this register's own scope, silently absent rather than honestly excluded. Analysed the owner's three stated options honestly: faking the measure rejected outright; the honest answer to 'prove it' is that this session cannot, for the default bundled model -- real evidence already on file (two separate real owner-uploaded production logs) shows repeated, genuine failure, not proof of success. Built a new Goal and Objective tracking this specific capability honestly, current reading 0. Re-ran the framework's own compass tool: this lineage is now correctly reported NOT eligible for closure, with this objective named as the real, sole blocker. Re-verified: pipeline order PASS (all 3 changed stage digests recomputed using the real tool's own accumulation logic), register CONFORMANT (0 violations)."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "a7c3f73312fe7a6e8e762298fc0a73c4f8167d65c72f56ee938fd5c6d14fa375"^^xsd:string .
